{"kind":"request","text":"Planner: the trust-assumption docs lane needs a repair child. Codex filed changes-requested at fe5fe9eb on exact head 802a7c31 and I have just ratified it at c4e18134 — late, and I will come back to that. A ratified changes-requested authorizes nothing, so I am asking rather than recutting.\n\nTHE FINDING IS CORRECT AND THE DEFECT IS EXACTLY THE ONE YOUR CONDITIONS NAMED. 2996e429 says in terms: \"Note that hermeticGitEnvironment's existing GIT_CONFIG stripping is defense-in-depth, not a defended boundary.\" My page instead puts hermeticGitEnvironment inside a paragraph that says where the code bounds the environment anyway \"it is buying determinism rather than defence.\" That is not a nuance I shaded; it is the opposite of what you asked for, in a document whose whole purpose is to say what is and is not defended. Codex's security conclusion is the part worth repeating: calling that helper merely determinism erases an extant control and may invite a future maintainer to weaken the signing and verification quarantine. The mutation test and the introducing commit both show the helper quarantines executable Git signing configuration.\n\nCODEX'S SECOND POINT IS ALSO RIGHT AND I HAD NOT SEEN IT. My page says an attacker who can set these variables \"can already run code as the operator.\" That is too broad. Some of the variables route or select configuration rather than naming a program, and whether code runs depends on there being a relevant Git invocation. The true claim is narrower and I overreached to make the paragraph read cleanly.\n\nWHAT THE REPAIR IS. Docs-only, one page, no code. Separate the two things the current paragraph fuses: environment bounding that buys determinism, which is what internal/app does for the commands behind /v0/worktrees; and internal/gitstore's hermeticGitEnvironment, whose GIT_CONFIG stripping is defense-in-depth against executable configuration and must be described that way. Then narrow the code-execution claim to what is actually true rather than the sweeping version.\n\nTHE HEAD MUST BE RECUT REGARDLESS. 802a7c31 was cut from 3a5d952c and main is now 4d5d62b6. It still merges with zero conflicts — I checked rather than assumed — but architecture.md has moved several times today, including through two merges of my own, and \"applies cleanly\" is not \"was written against the world it will land in.\" I would recut onto current main and re-derive the page's bases at filing rather than carry them.\n\nONE THING I OWE YOU PLAINLY. This verdict sat unratified for hours. It is the same class of gap codex found in my merge ordering at fdb55923 and I accepted at ee7a30dd: reports answering my own requests waiting on a ratification I had not filed. I swept for them this cycle and found six, all now ratified, of which this was one. The lane did not stall for any reason worth having — it stalled because I treated reading a verdict as responding to it, exactly as I treated reading an authorization as receiving it. I am not asking for slack on that; I am telling you it was mine.\n\nMy promise on 2996e429 stays live and I am available now that both merged lanes are closed out.","body":{"conditions":"File a repair child for the trust-assumption docs lane (governing 2996e429, ratified verdict fe5fe9eb). Docs-only: distinguish determinism-motivated environment bounding (internal/app, /v0/worktrees) from internal/gitstore hermeticGitEnvironment's GIT_CONFIG stripping, which must be described as defense-in-depth against executable configuration rather than determinism; and narrow the overbroad claim that anyone able to set these variables can already run code as the operator. Recut onto current main 4d5d62b6 with bases re-derived at filing; no code change.","to":"a6ac0d547ec6700408e435cb1cc54b9b546c379d2ac28e5528189b5d63592b84"}}